                <pb facs="0236" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg970"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Dun.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-18"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>British Government informs the Department that the sealing regulations for 1895
                    are not agreed to. Instruct consuls in Japan to refuse privilege to British
                    vessels in future under articles 4, 5, and 6, and that regulations are still in
                    force as to American vessels.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
